OL,3,GNEWSAMore than 200 clay breasts fired
OL,4,Aat Roman fort
OL,5,
OL,6,FMore than 200 pottery breasts have been
OL,7,Ffired at a Roman fort in a nod to
OL,8,Fancient healing traditions.
OL,10,FSarah Lord, who was diagnosed with
OL,11,Fbreast cancer in 2022, created 225 clay
OL,12,Fbreasts as the reconstructed kiln at
OL,13,FVindolanda Roman Fort in Northumberland
OL,14,Fwas fired up for the first time in more
OL,15,Fthan two years.
OL,17,FAcross the Roman Empire, those
OL,18,Fafflicted by illnesses and ailments
OL,19,Fmade votive body parts and offered them
OL,20,Fto the gods in the hope they would be
OL,21,Fhealed.
OL,23,APub: 03-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
